<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amarsinhji of Wankaner</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amarsinhji was the ruler, with the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> Sahib, of Wankaner, a princely state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhala">Jhala Rajputs</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, from 1881 to 1948. He modernised the state's administration and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-vilas-palace">Ranjit Vilas Palace</a>, completed in 1914, which mixes Indian and European styles. His rule ended when Wankaner was merged into the United State of Saurashtra in 1948.</p></div>
